  "notes": "The passenger oryx scheme with 'CARGO' added under 'QATAR': drawn from 777F A7-BFY (right side, 2026-06-27, nose to the right; titles read the same on both sides). Title places measured on the 777F, so they differ from the passenger file's (measured on longer types). Winglets: the 777F has raked tips in gray, so the burgundy winglet entry applies only if a type with winglets joins. Small Qatar flag above the forward cargo door not drawn. Every current freighter is a 777F (the 747-8Fs left in 2024); airframes are tagged in airframes/QTR.json. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the Arabic title's length (0.09) is the A350's 5.7 m taken onto the 777F (low); the oryx's outlines are smooth.",
  "history": "Qatar Airways Cargo's 777Fs (first, A7-BFA, in service 2010-05-18) have worn the 2006 oryx scheme with the CARGO title since delivery; the A330Fs and 747-8Fs that wore it have left the fleet."
